
## Rails-Specific

### Architecture
<!-- setup.sh replaces this based on detection -->
- **Pattern:** {{RAILS_ARCHITECTURE}} <!-- MVC / Service Objects / CQRS -->
- **API mode:** {{API_MODE}} <!-- yes/no -->
- **Frontend:** {{FRONTEND}} <!-- Hotwire / React / API-only -->

### Key Paths

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `app/models/` | ActiveRecord models |
| `app/controllers/` | Request handling |
| `app/services/` | Business logic (if using service objects) |
| `app/jobs/` | Background jobs |
| `db/migrate/` | Database migrations |
| `spec/` or `test/` | Tests |
| `config/routes.rb` | Route definitions |

### Testing
- **Framework:** {{TEST_FRAMEWORK}} <!-- RSpec / Minitest -->
- **Run all:** `{{TEST_COMMAND}}`
- **Run specific:** `{{TEST_COMMAND}} <path>`
- **System tests:** `{{TEST_COMMAND}} spec/system` or `bin/rails test:system`

### Style
- **Linter:** RuboCop (`bundle exec rubocop`)
- **Config:** `.rubocop.yml`
- **Auto-fix:** `bundle exec rubocop -a`

### Rails Gotchas
- **N+1 queries:** Always use `includes`/`preload` for associations in loops
- **Migration safety:** Never remove columns in the same deploy that removes code references. Use `ignored_columns` first.
- **Strong params:** Every controller action that accepts input must use strong parameters
- **Callbacks:** Avoid `after_save` for side effects — use service objects or jobs instead
- **Scopes:** Prefer scopes over class methods for query building

### Database
- **DB:** {{DATABASE}} <!-- PostgreSQL / MySQL / SQLite -->
- **Migrate:** `bin/rails db:migrate`
- **Rollback:** `bin/rails db:rollback`
- **Seed:** `bin/rails db:seed`
